sequenceDiagram
  %% docs/reference/tools.md#apt-repositories
  %% status: draft
  %% command: tool:apt-repository-add
  %% kind: tool.apt_repository_add
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>control Node
  participant N as Node 12<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: tool:apt-repository-add<br/>--node=12 --name=rex
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit tool:apt-repository-add --node=12 --name=rex --definition='{"uris":[…],"suites":["preview"],"components":["main"],"signing_key":{…}}'`
  %%> - syntax: `--node=ID --name=NAME --definition=JSON [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Validate, record rex<br/>adding · task #5140
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12, which runs the apt manager; no other apt write holds Node 12
  %%> - no other repository of Node 12 has one of its URIs and suites (`tool.repository_conflict`)
  %%> - a name keeps its definition until its removal succeeds (`tool.repository_conflict`); the same definition republishes it
  %%> - file mode takes the definition only from the catalog (`tool.not_in_catalog`, `tool.file_override`)
  GW->>SW: Start the Tools phase<br/>with only this repository
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5140
  SW->>N: Hold its preference<br/>to its owned Tools
  SW->>N: Verify the key, write<br/>keyring and source
  %%> Key:
  %%> - the downloaded key has exactly the recorded primary fingerprint, or `tool.repository_key_mismatch` before any keyring or source write
  SW->>N: Read its package index
  alt published
    SW-->>GW: Report rex ready
    Note over GW: rex: ready
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Tool writes from rex are admitted from now on
  else key, fetch or write failed
    SW--xGW: Report rex failed<br/>error_code
    Note over GW: rex: failed with the code
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again, or converge the Node; both run this publication
    %%> - a run that never started leaves the repository as it was; a timed-out one leaves it failed
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5140
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
